# cdda_hq.phases.pdl - scripted playthrough of cdda-hq through its REAL verbs (roadmap C3). Format: BOOK 06-testing/GAME-PLAYTHROUGH-HARNESSES.md
# Header rows:  GAME | <folder under @.apps> | <binary base name>      INIT | <path in the game folder> | <text>      NEEDS | <path under $HOUSE> | <dst under $T, default same>
# A phase:      PHASE | <id> | <title> | <extra keywords>       then rows until the next PHASE:
#   DO | verb | args...      run the game binary         PUT | path | text         write a file in the game folder (state surgery: say so in a NOTE)
#   SAY / NOSAY / SAYIS | text | label       the last DO's output contains / lacks / equals
#   HAS / LACKS / FILEIS | path | text | label      EXISTS / NOFILE | path | label      COUNT | path | line-prefix | n | label      UI | key | value | label      UIKEY | key | label
#   MARK | var | path | key    CAP | var    DELTA | before | after | n | label    EQ / NE | var | var | label    CP | src | dst    SUM | var | dir
GAME | cdda-hq | cdda_hq
# the skin text-includes the shared petslike core and its helpers (the scratch house has only what is listed; added 2026-11-04: the table predates the shared core and its setup no longer built)
NEEDS | &.widgits/world-ops/ops/+x/wo.+x
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/petslike_core.c
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/petslike_toolbar.c
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/pet_sky.c
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/pet_footer.c
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/pet_nudge.c
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/kh_state_notify.h
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/csv_frames.c
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/petslike_skin_lib.c
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/petslike_autotile.c
NEEDS | &.widgits/_shared-lib/petslike_life.c
CFLAGS | -I$T/@.apps/cdda-hq/ops
INIT | cdda-hq-pchq/pieces/system/maps/.keep | scratch board folder (export3d makes only the last two levels, so the parents must exist)\n
INIT | state/flag_int.txt | 1
INIT | state/flag_running.txt | 1
INIT | state/active.txt | rex\n
INIT | state/pet_rex.txt | room=castle\nx=2\ny=3\ndir=3\nsteps=1\ntx=-1\nty=-1\n

PHASE | p1_scavenge | scavenge two rags and see them in the bag, the ledger and the Inventory tab | bag, rag, inventory
DO | bag
SAY | bag empty | empty-bag-at-start
DO | craft | bandage
SAY | need the inputs | craft-refused-without-rag
DO | scavenge
SAY | found a rag | first-scavenge
DO | scavenge
SAY | found a rag | second-scavenge
DO | bag
SAYIS | rag 2 | bag-holds-two-rags
DO | inventory
SAY | rex:rag=2 | ledger-replay-says-two-rags
UI | n_inv | 1 | inventory-tab-has-one-row
UI | inv_0_label | rag x2 | inventory-tab-row-is-rag-x2
HAS | state/chat.txt | Rex finds a rag | chat-logs-the-find

PHASE | p2_craft | craft a bandage: one rag becomes a bandage and the clock moves by the recipe minutes | craft, recipe, bandage, clock
DO | clock | rate | hour
MARK | c0 | state/clock_root/#.desktop/clocks/rpg.pdl | game_time_epoch_ms
DO | craft | bandage
SAY | crafted bandage | craft-succeeds
MARK | c1 | state/clock_root/#.desktop/clocks/rpg.pdl | game_time_epoch_ms
DELTA | c0 | c1 | 60000 | clock-advanced-exactly-one-minute
DO | bag
SAYIS | rag 1, bandage 1 | bag-after-craft
UI | n_craft | 1 | craft-tab-has-the-recipe
UI | craft_0_label | Craft bandage 1m | craft-tab-row-shows-minutes
UI | inv_1_label | bandage x1 | inventory-tab-shows-the-bandage

PHASE | p3_door | walk through the castle stair door to the cellar | door, step, cellar, room
NOTE | state surgery: put Rex on the cell below the castle's stair door (the same start as XO/test_cdda_c1.sh)
PUT | state/pet_rex.txt | room=castle\nx=2\ny=3\ndir=3\nsteps=1\ntx=-1\nty=-1\n
DO | step | 0 | -1
SAY | now in the Cellar | door-message
HAS | state/pet_rex.txt | room=cellar | rex-is-in-the-cellar
COUNT | state/chat.txt | D[0-9]* [0-9:]* Rex moves to the Cellar$ | 1 | stamped-moves-to-the-line
UI | look_3_label | to Castle | look-tab-lists-the-way-back

PHASE | p4_strike | strike the zed twice: the wound rows change and the zed answers | strike, wounds, zed, body
NOTE | state surgery: zed one cell below Rex (the cellar default spot is 6,7)
PUT | state/zed.txt | room=cellar\nx=6\ny=7\ndir=0\n
PUT | state/pet_rex.txt | room=cellar\nx=6\ny=6\ndir=3\nsteps=1\ntx=-1\nty=-1\n
DO | wounds
SAYIS | nobody here is wounded | no-wounds-yet
DO | strike
SAY | zed | first-strike-reports-the-zed
DO | wounds
SAY | zed | wounds-lists-the-zed
CAP | w1
HAS | state/wounds.pdl | WOUND \p zed | wound-table-has-zed-rows
HAS | state/chat.txt | the zed hits Rex | zed-answers
DO | strike
DO | wounds
CAP | w2
NE | w1 | w2 | wounds-differ-after-the-second-strike
UI | n_body | 6 | body-tab-has-six-parts

PHASE | p5_saveload | save to slot 2, new game wipes the bag and wounds, load slot 2 brings them back | save, load, newgame, slot
DO | inventory
CAP | inv_saved
DO | save | 2
SAY | saved to slot 2 | save-reports-slot-2
DO | newgame
SAY | new game started | newgame-reports
DO | bag
SAY | bag empty | newgame-empties-the-bag
NOFILE | state/wounds.pdl | newgame-removes-wounds
DO | load | 2
SAY | loaded from slot 2 | load-reports-slot-2
DO | inventory
CAP | inv_loaded
EQ | inv_saved | inv_loaded | load-restores-the-same-bags
EXISTS | state/wounds.pdl | load-brings-wounds-back

PHASE | p6_replay | a fresh game fed the same event ledger replays to the same bags | replay, ledger, determinism
DO | inventory
CAP | inv_before
CP | state/events.txt | state/events.keep
DO | newgame
DO | inventory
SAY | (nothing) | fresh-game-has-nothing
CP | state/events.keep | state/events.txt
DO | inventory
CAP | inv_replayed
EQ | inv_before | inv_replayed | replay-equals-the-original
COUNT | state/events.txt | EVENT\p | 8 | ledger-has-the-event-rows

PHASE | p7_clock_load | save, move the clock on, load: the game clock is back where it was saved (fix 2026-11-04: load used to leave it ahead) | clock, save, load
DO | clock | advance | 2h
MARK | c0 | state/clock_root/#.desktop/clocks/rpg.pdl | game_time_epoch_ms
DO | save | 9
SAY | saved | save-says-saved
DO | clock | advance | 3h
MARK | c1 | state/clock_root/#.desktop/clocks/rpg.pdl | game_time_epoch_ms
DELTA | c0 | c1 | 10800000 | control-the-advance-moved-the-clock-three-hours
DO | load | 9
MARK | c2 | state/clock_root/#.desktop/clocks/rpg.pdl | game_time_epoch_ms
EQ | c0 | c2 | load-restored-the-saved-clock
NE | c1 | c2 | the-clock-really-moved-back-from-the-advanced-value

PHASE | p8_lamps | a bought lamp lights its room while lamps are on and not when they are off (shared code, petslike_core.c) | lamps, light, 3d book
DO | buy | lamp
SAY | Lamp pillar | lamp-bought-and-placed
DO | lamps | on
SAY | lamps on | lamps-verb-answers
EXISTS | cdda-hq-pchq/pieces/system/maps/cdda-hq/game.pdl | export3d-wrote-the-book
HAS | state/house.txt | lamp | house-ledger-has-the-lamp
EXISTS | lamps.pdl | lamps-pdl-is-in-the-scratch-game
HAS | cdda-hq-pchq/pieces/system/maps/cdda-hq/city/lights.pdl | LIGHT | lamps-on-writes-a-light-row-for-the-lamp
DO | lamps | off
NOFILE | cdda-hq-pchq/pieces/system/maps/cdda-hq/city/lights.pdl | lamps-off-removes-the-light-file
